// 	This file's purpose is to contain the contract test methods for each public method in ArrayList.
// 	Included methods are: Add, Remove, and Insert. 
// 	Each contract test method is based on assumptions in order to test each public method. The assumptions involve parameters and the state of the object in question (arrList in this case). All the assumptions are tested using the PexAssumeUnderTest attribute.
// 	Contract tests check the list's properties (index of x, last index of x, count, and whether it contains x) after each operation. The PexObserve.ValueForViewing method is used to output the values for viewing in the IDE.
// 	The test is performed by a test method that runs the given operation (add, remove, or insert) on the given list and checks all properties before and after the operation. 
// 	Assertions are used to validate the tests – by asserting that the size of the ArrayList increases by one after an add operation is performed.
//	The contract tests can be run and seen in the visual studio unit test viewer. 
// 	Please make sure you run tests by setting the 'Run state' to 'All tests' from the configuration manager.
//  Make sure test cases are in a state that doesn't interfere with your code by unchecking 'Reset state' on the test cases menu.
